路径（改为多阶段构建）、JuheQqIdentityProvider 中未使用的 Objects import\\\\n  - 第一轮修复了：LeaderboardServiceTest 路径 test/test/→test/java/ 和 import ConditionalAuthorizationManager.when→Mockito.when\\\\n  - 旧 jar keycloak-social-provider-china-1.0.0.jar 已从 docker/keycloak/ 删除，Dockerfile 已移除其 COPY 行\\\\n  - 确认无其他地方引用旧 jar\\\\n  - JuheQqIdentityProvider.java 不再有 java.util.Objects import\\\\n\\\\nEFFORT: medium\\\\nSTOP_CONDITION: 完成全部 6 项检查，报告 0 新问题或列出残留问题\\\\nOUTPUT:\\\\n  VERDICT: 通过 / 有问题\\\\n  EVIDENCE: 逐项列出\\\\n  GAPS:\\\\n  NEXT:\\\",\\n-        \\\"role\\\": \\\"verifier\\\"\\n-      },\\n-      \\\"model\\\": \\\"deepseek-v4-flash\\\",\\n-      \\\"nickname\\\": \\\"带齿喙鲸\\\",\\n-      \\\"status\\\": \\\"Completed\\\",\\n-      \\\"result\\\": \\\"Now I have all the information needed. Let me compile the complete verification report.\\\\n\\\\n### SUMMARY\\\\n\\\\nCompleted second-round Grill-Fix review of all Juhe QQ Identity Provider changes across all 11 scoped files. **Found 3 new issues**: (1) `deploy.yml` still downloads and mounts the old `keycloak-social-provider-china-1.0.0.jar` as `keycloak-qq.jar` instead of building the custom `Dockerfile.keycloak` image, (2) `.gitignore` still has a stale `!docker/keycloak/*.jar` exception for the old jar, and (3) the `LeaderboardServiceTest.java` file is still under `test/test/` rather than `test/java/` (path was NOT actually fixed). All first-round fixes (Dockerfile multi-stage build, removed `java.util.Objects` import, removed `ConditionalAuthorizationManager` references) are confirmed correct.\\\\n\\\\n### EVIDENCE\\\\n\\\\n- **Check 1 — Old jar残留引用**: FOUND 2 stale references.\\\\n  - `.github/workflows/deploy.yml:117` volume-mounts `./keycloak-qq.jar:/opt/keycloak/providers/keycloak-qq.jar` — still using the old third-party jar\\\\n  - `.github/workflows/deploy.yml:145-146` `curl -fSL -o keycloak-qq.jar https://github.com/trashblazer/keycloak-social-provider-china/releases/download/v1.0.0/keycloak-social-provider-china-1.0.0.jar`