\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **Check 1 — Old jar残留引用**: FOUND 2 stale references.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  - `.github/workflows/deploy.yml:117` volume-mounts `./keycloak-qq.jar:/opt/keycloak/providers/keycloak-qq.jar` — still using the old third-party jar\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  - `.github/workflows/deploy.yml:145-146` `curl -fSL -o keycloak-qq.jar https://github.com/trashblazer/keycloak-social-provider-china/releases/download/v1.0.0/keycloak-social-provider-china-1.0.0.jar` — still downloads the old jar for production deployment\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  - `.gitignore:33-35` has stale `# keycloak provider JAR 需要随仓库走...` comment and `!docker/keycloak/*.jar` exception — no longer needed since `docker/keycloak/` no longer contains jar files (only `wotbtools-realm.json`)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  - `docker/keycloak/` dir confirmed: only `wotbtools-realm.json` remains (via `list_dir`), old jar is gone\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **Check 2 — Dockerfile一致性**: PASS.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  - `docker/Dockerfile.keycloak` (lines 1-10) uses multi-stage build: `FROM maven:3.9-eclipse-temurin-21 AS build`, copies `java/pom.xml`, `java/settings-docker.xml`, `java/keycloak-juhe-qq-provider/pom.xml` and `src`, runs `mvn -s settings-docker.xml -pl keycloak-juhe-qq-provider -DskipTests clean package -q`, then `FROM quay.io/keycloak/keycloak:26.6.4` and `COPY --from=build` the built jar\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  - `docker/online/docker-compose.yml:12-15` correctly uses `build: context: ../../ dockerfile: docker/Dockerfile.keycloak` (builds from source, no jar download)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  - **IMPORTANT**: deploy.yml (production) does NOT use `Dockerfile.keycloak` — it uses the old `quay.io/keycloak/keycloak:26.6.3` image with the old jar mounted — this is a production inconsistency with the local docker-compose setup\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **Check 3 — import正确性**: PASS for source files, but deploy.yml references non-existent import flow.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  - `JuheQqIdentityProvider.java`: 20 imports — all used in code, no `java.util.Objects`, no `ConditionalAuthorizationManager`. Verified: `JsonNode`, `ObjectMapper`, `Response`, `UriInfo`, `Logger`, `AbstractIdentityProvider`, `AuthenticationCallback`, `AuthenticationRequest`, `BrokeredIdentityContext`, `EventBuilder`, `KeycloakSession`, `RealmModel`, `IOException`, `URI`, `URLEncoder`, `HttpClient`, `HttpRequest`, `HttpResponse`, `StandardCharsets`, `Duration` — all accounted for\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  - `JuheQqIdentityProviderFactory.java`: imports `AbstractIdentityProviderFactory`, `IdentityProviderModel`, `KeycloakSession`, `ProviderConfigProperty`, `ArrayList`, `List` — all correct\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  - `JuheQqIdentityProviderConfig.java`: imports `IdentityProviderModel` — correct\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  - `LeaderboardServiceTest.java`: all 10 imports are correct (`LeaderboardRecordRepository`, `LeaderboardService`, `Battle`, `PlayerResult`, `Tankopedia`, `OffsetDateTime`, `ZoneOffset`, `ArrayList`, `List`, `Optional`, plus static `assertEquals`, `assertNotNull`, `mock`, `never`, `verify`, `when`, `any`, `anyLong`, `eq`). No `ConditionalAuthorizationManager`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  - `useAuth.js`: Vue/Keycloak imports correct\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **Check 4 — 路径正确性**: 1 REMAINING ISSUE.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  - `LeaderboardServiceTest.java` file is at `java/wotb-web/src/test/test/com/wotb/web/LeaderboardServiceTest.java` — still under `test/test/` NOT `test/java/`. The first-round claim \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"path test/test/→test/java/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" was not actually executed; the file was not moved.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  - All other scoped file paths verified as correct (each `read_file` succeeded for the paths listed in SCOPE, except the test file which needed the `test/test/` variant)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  - `settings-docker.xml` exists at `java/settings-docker.xml` — referenced correctly by both `Dockerfile.keycloak` and `Dockerfile.backend`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **Check 5 — JuheQqIdentityProvider.java no `java.util.Objects`**: CONFIRMED PASS. grep returned zero matches for the `keycloak-juhe-qq-provider` directory.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **Check 6 — POM consistency**: PASS.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  - `java/pom.xml` includes `<module>keycloak-juhe-qq-provider</module>` — correct\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  - Module POM at `java/keycloak-juhe-qq-provider/pom.xml` has correct `<parent>` ref to `com.wotb:wotb-parent:1.0.0`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\