d `wotb-web`, not the keycloak provider module). **This Docker build will fail at `COPY` time.**\\\\\\\\n  - **PROBLEM B**: `frontend/src/composables/useAuth.js:10-13` — The Keycloak URL is hard-coded to `https://auth.wotbtools.com`. This prevents local/offline development where Keycloak runs on `http://localhost:8080`. There is no environment variable or build-time configuration to override this.\\\\\\\\n  - **PROBLEM C**: `java/keycloak-juhe-qq-provider/pom.xml:43-47` — The `keycloak-services` dependency at scope `provided` is unusual; typically `keycloak-server-spi-private` is sufficient. However, since the code only references classes from `keycloak-server-spi` and `keycloak-server-spi-private` (no direct `keycloak-services` types), this is likely harmless but slightly over-broad.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### CHANGES\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nNone.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### RISKS\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- **Broken Docker build (docker/Dockerfile.keycloak:2)**: The `COPY` of `keycloak-juhe-qq-provider.jar` will fail because the jar is never built and does not exist in the source tree. **Mitigation**: Add a multi-stage build step in the Dockerfile to build the provider jar from source (similar to how `Dockerfile.backend` builds the backend), or pre-build and commit the jar, or modify the Dockerfile to reference the jar from the Maven build output.\\\\\\\\n- **Hard-coded production Keycloak URL (frontend/src/composables/useAuth.js:11)**: Local developers must manually edit this file to test against a local Keycloak instance. **Mitigation**: Use a build-time environment variable (e.g., Vite `import.meta.env.VITE_KEYCLOAK_URL`) with the production URL as default but overridable in `.env.development`.\\\\\\\\n- **Unused keycloak-services dependency (pom.xml:43-47)**: While harmless at `provided` scope, it creates a minor maintenance burden and potential confusion about module boundaries. **Mitigation**: Remove if no direct code dependency exists, or add a comment explaining why it is needed.\\\\\