r/keycloak/*.jar` exception — no longer needed since `docker/keycloak/` no longer contains jar files (only `wotbtools-realm.json`)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  - `docker/keycloak/` dir confirmed: only `wotbtools-realm.json` remains (via `list_dir`), old jar is gone\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **Check 2 — Dockerfile一致性**: PASS.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  - `docker/Dockerfile.keycloak` (lines 1-10) uses multi-stage build: `FROM maven:3.9-eclipse-temurin-21 AS build`, copies `java/pom.xml`, `java/settings-docker.xml`, `java/keycloak-juhe-qq-provider/pom.xml` and `src`, runs `mvn -s settings-docker.xml -pl keycloak-juhe-qq-provider -DskipTests clean package -q`, then `FROM quay.io/keycloak/keycloak:26.6.4` and `COPY --from=build` the built jar\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  - `docker/online/docker-compose.yml:12-15` correctly uses `build: context: ../../ dockerfile: docker/Dockerfile.keycloak` (builds from source, no jar download)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  - **IMPORTANT**: deploy.yml (production) does NOT use `Dockerfile.keycloak` — it uses the old `quay.io/keycloak/keycloak:26.6.3` image with the old jar mounted — this is a production inconsistency with the local docker-compose setup\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- **Check 3 — import正确性**: PASS for source files, but deploy.yml references non-existent import flow.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  - `JuheQqIdentityProvider.java`: 20 imports — all used in code, no `java.util.Objects`, no `ConditionalAuthorizationManager`. Verified: `JsonNode`, `ObjectMapper`, `Response`, `UriInfo`, `Logger`, `AbstractIdentityProvider`, `AuthenticationCallback`